=== Part 1: the P3a observation point -- the candidate's OWN timing fit, descriptive only ===
OK   THE SOURCE IS THE CANDIDATE ITSELF: each P contention event carries exactly the `timingFit` of the candidate that attempted that interval (GOOD for 10:00, BEST for 10:30) -- read at the rejection point, not recomputed or joined
OK   a candidate with NO timing fit yields an event with NO `timingFit` key (absent, never a guess), and a FIXED target (no candidate exists) carries none
OK   EMISSION UNCHANGED: the same candidates with and without timing fits yield the identical event sequence by event identity (same count, owners, intervals, rounds) -- only the descriptive payload differs
OK   CONSTRUCTOR BEHAVIOR UNCHANGED: the traced result equals the plain `constructDay` result byte-for-byte (the payload is observational and write-only)
OK   the event contract is the old one plus the optional descriptive field: exactly loserIntentId, winnerIntentId, attemptedStart, attemptedEnd, winnerStart, winnerEnd, round, timingFit; the key set is detached strings (no Date, no candidate)
OK   CANDIDATE ORDER AUDIT: two attempts with equal timingFit and equal start place the SAME interval with the SAME fit, so `candidateOrder` can only label which duplicate was chosen -- it is not carried
=== Part 2: directed fixtures on the REAL orchestrator ===
OK   GOOD VS BEST (neutral ranking): P attempted GOOD@10:00 (trace order first) and BEST@11:30 (second); the authority carries both exact fits
OK   TRACE ORDER != NEUTRAL RANKING: the real `compareCandidatesForPlacement`, fed from the authority payload alone, ranks BEST@11:30 FIRST although the trace discovered GOOD@10:00 first
OK   the promotion contention view carries the same fits, per authorized owner (A for 10:00, B for 11:30)
OK   P MISSING-INTERMEDIATE REGRESSION: 10:00 is NOT in P's initial list (10:30 only) and NOT in its final list (empty), and IS in the scheduling attempt authority with its exact fit (GOOD) against B
OK   INITIAL-ONLY OWNER: B's 11:30 is available from the basis INITIAL list and not from its final list; B's terminal 10:00 is available from the basis FINAL list -- the attempts supplement, they do not replace, the basis
OK   UNION DEDUP: B's 11:30 appears in the basis (initial) AND as an attempt, with the same (start, timingFit) identity -- one scheduling choice, not two
OK   DIRECTED COUNTEREXAMPLE REPRODUCED (real orchestrator): X@13:00, Y@10:00, O@11:00 placed; P Deferred; P's authorized owners are X, Y and O
OK   MISSING FROM BASIS: O's 09:30 is ABSENT from O's initialCandidates (13:30) and from O's finalCandidates (11:00) -- it lived only in an intermediate replenishment list
